# Content authoring

- A new kind of gameplay content is a ScriptableObject definition plus its
  authored assets. Keep tunable balance and catalog data in those assets, not
  hardcoded in runtime code.
- A repeated UI row, card, slot, or world view is one prefab with instances or
  a pool; do not copy its hierarchy into multiple bespoke objects.
- Fixed-count UI slots are authored and pre-placed. Variable lists use an
  authored child-view prefab under a serialized parent and pool instances.
- Preserve asset GUIDs and serialized references when moving assets. Use
  Unity-aware asset operations where available; do not hand-recreate YAML
  references.
- Do not import catalog content merely because source data exists. Respect the
  gameplay-ready set, deferred mechanics, and release scope in
  `planning/handoff.md`.
